    {
      "id": "1Sj22VUKlFcVSoXA_hbfD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 237.77659062020348,
      "y": 444.99988681284844,
      "width": 991.8997192382812,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 115357993,
      "version": 2017,
      "versionNonce": 450320320,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764093063977,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How did I used to build AI systems?\n\n1. Define the task.\n2. Collect training data / samples of 'good' input -> output pairs.\n3. Design evals to measure how well a prediction fits with \n   the expected behavior.\n4. Stitch one or more open source HF models together to get a baseline.\n5. Iterate on the system architecture and parameter choices, \n   hill-climb towards the 'best' solution.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How did I used to build AI systems?\n\n1. Define the task.\n2. Collect training data / samples of 'good' input -> output pairs.\n3. Design evals to measure how well a prediction fits with \n   the expected behavior.\n4. Stitch one or more open source HF models together to get a baseline.\n5. Iterate on the system architecture and parameter choices, \n   hill-climb towards the 'best' solution.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
