      "versionNonce": 596473792,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764093084853,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Observations\n**THESE ARE ANECDOTES, NOT BENCHMARK RESULTS**\n\n- For this task, most *good* models performed similar.\n- Lots of variance between different runs on the same model\n- Cursor and OpenCode performed similarly (this is a simple codebase,\n  remember)\n- Agents often give up too early or focus too much on parameter, rather\n  than method choice. A better approach would be for the agent to do a\n  more exploratory search first, then tune parameters on high-performing\n  methods.\n- Running the whole system completely end to end yields worse results than\n  directing the coding agents over multiple messages.\n- It gets expensive\n\nTips\n\n- Write analysis scripts that fit with your particular task. The QA images \n  improved performance.\n- If you want the model to think longer, say \"the current best solution is \n  X%, you must beat it\". Can lead to costly loops, though\n- Try and encourage emergent behaviour by instructing the model to write its\n  own analysis scripts, where neccessary.\n\nFuture\n\n- Proper analysis of performance across models, proper ablation studies\n- Try on other tasks such as chat agents. More to come here",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Observations\n**THESE ARE ANECDOTES, NOT BENCHMARK RESULTS**\n\n- For this task, most *good* models performed similar.\n- Lots of variance between different runs on the same model\n- Cursor and OpenCode performed similarly (this is a simple codebase,\n  remember)\n- Agents often give up too early or focus too much on parameter, rather\n  than method choice. A better approach would be for the agent to do a\n  more exploratory search first, then tune parameters on high-performing\n  methods.\n- Running the whole system completely end to end yields worse results than\n  directing the coding agents over multiple messages.\n- It gets expensive\n\nTips\n\n- Write analysis scripts that fit with your particular task. The QA images \n  improved performance.\n- If you want the model to think longer, say \"the current best solution is \n  X%, you must beat it\". Can lead to costly loops, though\n- Try and encourage emergent behaviour by instructing the model to write its\n  own analysis scripts, where neccessary.\n\nFuture\n\n- Proper analysis of performance across models, proper ablation studies\n- Try on other tasks such as chat agents. More to come here",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
